# Code owners for MetaMask skills.
#
# Domain teams maintain their skills. Platform teams own shared tooling,
# documentation, and anything without a more specific owner.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so order matters: fallbacks first,
# specific domain owners next, self-protection last.

# Default fallback.
*                        @MetaMask/extension-platform @MetaMask/mobile-platform

# By default, executable files in distributable paths require security review.
# This rule is intended as a fallback and can be overridden by subsequent lines.
/domains/                @MetaMask/security-liaisons @MetaMask/policy-reviewers
/domains/**/scripts/     @MetaMask/application-security @MetaMask/security-liaisons @MetaMask/policy-reviewers
/domains/**/adapters/    @MetaMask/application-security @MetaMask/security-liaisons @MetaMask/policy-reviewers

# By default, markdown files in distributable paths do not require codeowner review.
# This rule is intended as a fallback, and can be overridden by subsequent lines.
/domains/**/*.md
/domains/**/*.mdc

# Shared tooling and documentation.
